 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or later to be in the path. It can be found in the
 WHDLoad package.
 XFDDecrunch must also be in the path for installation. It is available in
 aminet:util/pack/xfdmaster.lha.

 Install from the three DOS disks named "Red Baron #1", "Red Baron #2"
 and "Red Baron #3", in any drive. DOS disk images can also be mounted
 using DiskImage; the installer lists the required tools.
 The copy-protected MFM release is not supported.
 Installer 44.10 or later enables icon previews and drawer opening.

 The tested minimum is 0.5 MB ChipMem and 2 MB FastMem.
 It can be quit by pressing num '*' (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate requester.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive 
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.

 The slave reserves 1 MB for game and renderer memory, plus Kickstart.
 The former 512 KB ChipMem + 1.5 MB slow-RAM configuration is insufficient.
 Tested minimum: 512 KB ChipMem + 2 MB FastMem (normal-build flight).
 Faster rendering releases the 192 KB game-pool extension for sim v1.
 With the option off, the game retains its original allocation budget.
 DMA allocations retain their original ChipMem requests.
 Faster rendering enables instruction caching on 020+ where needed.
 It does not enable a disabled data cache. On a 68030 with an MMU, use
 the MMU tooltype to permit fast-memory data caching; ChipMem stays uncached.
 Current maximum-detail measurements show less than 2% difference with MMU,
 below the resolution of the FPS window; no speedup is claimed for the tooltype.

 Features:
 ---------
 - FastMem and CPU cache support, keyboard fixes and mission-tape saving.
 - English and German releases supported; Manual and Keys included.

 Rendering improvements:
 - Faster rendering is On by default (normal build: CUSTOM2=0). It selects the verified dashboard cache, geometry,
   solid-fill, persistent-gauge, static-artwork, scene and sound optimizations, with CPU-specific choices.
 - On 030/040/060, resource generations avoid rescanning unchanged cockpit
   bitmap and mask bytes. Mutable drawing inputs retain exact checks.
 - On 030/040/060, Faster rendering uses longword span fills and specialized
   line loops in FastMem. This adds no working buffers or RAM requirement.
 - With Faster rendering and Consistent game speed enabled on 040/060,
   scenery selection retains a separate presentation cache using the native
   camera-distance and view rules. Drawing restores the simulation copy.
   This uses about 76 KB additional FastMem when available; allocation failure
   retains the previous path. The minimum RAM requirement is unchanged.
 - Large W6 buffers are allocated only when enabled; interpolation buffers
   are allocated only on 020+. Verification snapshots are excluded from the
   normal build. Buffers are reused across missions; minimum RAM is unchanged.
 - On 060, and on 030/040 with Consistent game speed, changed gauge
   backgrounds use clipped CPU restores from FastMem.
   Unchanged gauges persist per page below the current scene and static artwork.
   Native needle callbacks and event redraws are retained. Allocation failure
   retains native drawing; RAM requirements are unchanged.
   Without Consistent game speed, 040 keeps its guarded cache and 030 uses
   native gauges. The 020 gauge path is unchanged.
 - On 030/040/060, the forward overlay and static cockpit artwork are composed
   in FastMem before the viewport copy. Artwork outside that viewport persists
   on each page and is repaired after redraws, messages, view/resource changes
   or page reuse. Firing, other views and cache misses retain the previous path.
   000/010/020 retain native artwork. The existing reserved FastMem and 8 KB
   ChipMem mask are reused; RAM requirements are unchanged.
 - On 040/060, and on 030 with Consistent game speed, supported convex
   polygons are drawn directly as planar spans
   in FastMem, avoiding scratch clear, edge/fill and merge passes. Native
   clipping, unusual polygons and outlines retain their existing paths.
   RAM requirements are unchanged.
 - On 030 with Consistent game speed, unchanged upper-viewport words skip
   the ChipMem copy. An optional 48,000-byte FastMem shadow allocation is
   reused across missions; allocation failure retains the full copy.
 - On 030/040/060, supported scene viewports are drawn in reserved FastMem
   and copied to ChipMem once. Direct primitives avoid repeated plane setup;
   old page pixels and scratch are not copied in or exported. Native clipping
   is retained, with native fallback for unsupported layouts.
   000/010/020 retain the native scene renderer. RAM requirements are unchanged.
 - On 030/040/060, FastMem scene work can overlap display scanning. ChipMem
   page reuse waits until the prior display has finished; copper pickup is guarded.
   Native frames and slower CPUs retain the original safe beam wait.
   The two-field cap remains (about 25 FPS on PAL). This does not make world
   speed frame-rate independent by itself.
 - Select Off in the splash window, or CUSTOM2=1, to disable it.
   This reverses the former development normal-build 0/1 meaning.
   Supplied icon tooltypes are unchanged.
 - Applies only to sim v1; v2/v3 retain their existing fixes.
 - The dashboard cache uses about 13.7 KB extra ChipMem, with allocation fallback.
 - With Consistent game speed Off, faster frames can accelerate the world
   on slow machines. Neither option changes the Time Scale setting.
 - Developer builds retain individual CUSTOM2 bits (CUSTOM2=0 disables all).
   They select consistent game speed with bit 13; CUSTOM3 is player-build only.
   Normal/developer builds
   contain no VERIFY instruments or scripted game input.

 Performance and Time Scale:
 - Consistent game speed is an independent opt-in splash option (CUSTOM3=1).
   It is Off by default (CUSTOM3=0), even with Faster rendering On. It works
   with Faster rendering Off too. Supported on 68000 and 020+; 68010 retains
   native timing. It enables safe presentation and a one-field cap, without
   promising 50 FPS. Time Scale is unchanged; overload drops excess world time.
   W6 release acceptance was completed by the user on 2026-10-13.
 - Measured W6 envelope: A500 Time Scale 0 passed the rate window;
   maximum-detail Time Scale 40 dropped simulation time. 020/030/040/060
   passed their Time Scale 40 rate windows. These are not full gameplay
   guarantees for every mission. Reduce detail on slower machines.

 History:
 --------
 version 3.0b (13.10.2026)
 - CPU-specific rendering improvements and optional consistent game speed
   as described above.
 - ReadMe and installer adapted to the WHDLoad Install Template, retaining
   JOTD's three-disk layout, executable decompression and icon choices.

 version 2.1 (26.11.2005) done by JOTD
 - german version supported
 - OS swaps removed (thanks Bert for the advice)

 version 2.0 (10.05.2005) done by JOTD
 - keyboard fixed
 - save tape to disk now works
 - 2 versions now properly supported

 version 1.2 (19.09.2003)
 - fixed access fault when replaying missions (happens in non-BTTR version)

 version 1.1
 - removed "tapes" check, not necessary
 - adapted for BTTR version (kickfs update was needed)
 - now requires WHDLoad v16
 - source code included

 version 1.0-B (10.04.03)
 - install script fixed, now creates the "tapes" directory
 - slave checks that the directory "tapes" exists in the data sub-directory
   (if you installed with v1.0, create this directory manually or reinstall)

 version 1.0 (30.03.03) done by JOTD:
 - initial release
 - fixed to work with fastmem and caches on 68060
 - manual included
 - icons by Exoticons & VC

 To do:
 - support the MFM version

 Contact:
 --------
 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, NOVBRMOVE, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page or create a mantis issue directly
 at http://mantis.whdload.de

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
	http://www.whdload.de/
 or	aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and	aminet:game/patch/
